    "turn_text": "Well, he has a right to do it, but here's his right to do. No, it's not like to do. Justice ought to run its course here. And I would say to my Republican friends, if any attempt is made to pardon this man, it would not be because he has any sympathy for him. It will be because he is trying to protect himself. And I believe that's what he would like to do. It's a short circuit through some investigation. If you don't want the American people to know how much polluting and whatever other criminality might have been taking place, he is trying to keep that from never coming to life. But I do believe that not only the justice prevail, I think the resilience of this country is going to prevail. And what that cannot happen as my colleagues did not step up and do their",
