    "turn_text": "Oh, I believe there's a right thing to do. They don't believe Donald Trump by any means. They know full well that this man is guilty of at least nine or eight percent of everything he's been accused of. They have just decided that he is the one person that was a liver for them, the kind of climate that they would like to see created in this country. This man is simply creating a climate in which we can roll the clock back on a lot of things. Now, you know, April, I say a lot that I would not be so concerned if I didn't know the history of this country, the way that I do. I remember the other day, someone saying something to me as well. This is Andrew Johnson all over again. Those I didn't know who I was talking about. That's the man that followed Lincoln into the presidency. He was Lincoln's vice president. He got on the ticket as a part of a deal to satisfy the southern states. uh... making a lot of people realize it was elected president or the republican uh... it was all of a fusion ticket uh... between uh... a southern uh... democrats ball intention purposes uh... and a republican marvellous and johnson was in place he set out to undo everything that they've done and he got impeached for And I think that what we've seen is the same thing taken place here. This man has decided to set out to undo everything Barack Obama ever did. And I really believe in the final analysis. He's either going to get indicted or impeached for it. He may get both.",
