    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43651.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "I think that what the Congress would do is what this Congress ought to be doing now. Have open hearings. I think that we ought to use this opportunity to have fair and open hearings and then go wherever the evidence leads. This old notion about moving for some kind of the impeachment. I don't think we'll do that. I think we will have effective oversight. And if that oversight yields the kind of thing that I'll lead to impeachment, so more to be. But this thing about just jumping and having impeachment vote, I would not advise the Congress to do that. I would advise us to do exactly what we're asking Republicans to do. have open and fair hearings and like people don't start trying to short circuit stuff like newness has been doing but have it so that everybody will come and make their positions known And then we found out where the money is gone and didn't need to just follow the money.",
