  {
    "episode_id": 43651,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43651.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "Well, surely I support Nancy Pelosi. I've already supported Nancy Pelosi and I would not challenge Nancy Pelosi. But if the situation were to develop that Nancy Pelosi decides that she cannot mount an effective candidate, say, I will be open to offering for leader, lawful speak of the House, whichever the Congressional Black Caucus thinks is the best to pursue. So that's where I am on that. And if I were to be so fortunate I would, as I said, move to transform our caucus. There's some things that we've got to do going forward that we are not doing enough of. Number one, we have got to stop letting consultants run our approaches to campaign it. One of the reasons we lost the last presidential election is because nobody would not listen to people with experiences, people who have boots on the ground, you only listen to the people who develop analytics. And they say, well, the analytics say this, analytics say that. I don't care what analytics say. You cannot, in politics, take the place of human beings, people who interact with other people. And so there's some things that we've got to do in our caucus without being open to doing. And so I'm not now putting together any kind of approach to this. We don't have enough time to do that. Right now, I mean, North Carolina, I just finished a congressional district 13. I'm on my way to congressional district 2 and 8. I've already been to congressional district 9. These are four congressional districts. In North Carolina, I think we've got a chance to win, and I'm trying to do everything I can to win them. As we can, I'll go to Florida. And then the first of next week, I'll go to Michigan. At the floor, the next five or six days of robo, I will have gone to 12 congressional districts trying to make sure that we get to have a turnout that we need to win on November 6.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "I support Nancy Pelosi.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Human interaction is essential in politics and cannot be replaced by data.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "I would not challenge Nancy Pelosi.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "We currently let consultants dictate our campaign strategies.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Analytics alone should not determine political strategy.",
        "confidence": 0.93
